From 91f48a91a20feb610379b1db54059947ca93b394 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:44:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Report background jobs an idle chat loses when the
 backend exits

A chat that starts terminal(background=true, notify=true) and ends its turn is
idle, so the update step-boundary pause never sees it. Skew retirement, the
updater restart, idle exit and a Desktop quit all end in _shutdown_sessions ->
agent.close -> kill(source=agent_close, consume_output=True): the notify the chat
waited on never arrived and nothing recorded why.

Before sessions are closed (atexit and the SIGTERM flush handler), each
session's owned non-persist running jobs are journaled into its turn marker
(write-ahead), stopped with source backend_shutdown and consume_output=False,
and their outcome journaled. A turn in flight keeps its crash marker and gains
the list. An idle session with a notify job gets a background_jobs_stopped
marker; the next backend's startup sweep / session.resume submits a turn listing
each job (id, UTC start, command head, restart advice) and its completion notice
naming the update or the shutdown. That receipt outlives the turn freshness
window (24 h). Real session ends and persist_on_release are unchanged.

Review round 1 of t_01a182eec0f3584b.
